# Regression: scrolling the sidebar list used to leave the rows in place but
# stop drawing their titles past a certain offset — the rows stayed clickable
# and went blank.
#
# It also pins the two things feat/vis-list2 changed about this list, because
# both of them are visible from here and nowhere else in the suite:
#
#   1. The list renders MORE than a viewport's worth of rows, so the scroll
#      view has something to move. It used to be capped at viewport-minus-one,
#      which made the panel's content shorter than the panel by construction —
#      the scroll was dead and the tail of the catalog sat behind a
#      "Show N more…" button that cost a row to save a row. That button is why
#      this script used to have to click `sb_show_more` before it could scroll
#      anything; there is nothing to expand now.
#   2. A row title gets the full column. The trailing star used to reserve 18px
#      on every row whether or not a star was ever drawn there, and the seventh
#      row's title is long enough to show it: "…, D1136…" with the reserve,
#      "…, D113637…" without. That exact string is the assertion below.
#
# Both titles are asserted in their SIDEBAR-ellipsized form. Every row title is
# also painted on a Home card in the main pane, at a width that does not
# ellipsize it, and a duplicate label satisfies expect_text wherever it is —
# so a bare title would pass with every sidebar row blank, which is the exact
# regression this script exists for (afterhours_gaps.md #73). The "…" is what
# makes the assertion about the sidebar.
#
# The bottom rows are addressed with assert_ui_text and a y, not expect_text:
# they are short enough that the sidebar never ellipsizes them, so their only
# distinguishing feature against the Home card carrying the same words is where
# they landed. Coordinates re-derived by rendering at this script's own window
# size and reading the PNG, not by arithmetic on the old ones.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}

expect_text "stickers broke — concluded, D113637…"
assert_ui_text "profiling the disk" y=306

mouse_move 140 600
scroll_wheel 0 -6
wait_frames 6
scroll_wheel 0 -6
wait_frames 6
scroll_wheel 0 -6
wait_frames 6
scroll_wheel 0 -6
wait_frames 10

# The list moved and the rows that came up with it are lettered, not blank.
# At the clamped bottom the last of the twenty sits here.
assert_ui_text "PSC daily post generator" y=706
